        "displayName": "Daphnis",
        "panel": {
          "introduction": "Daphnis travels inside the Keeler Gap in Saturn’s A ring. This tiny moon raises waves along the gap’s edges, while Cassini’s close views reveal ridges and a coating of fine material. The displayed 2026 orbit extrapolates a 2005–2018 fit; Horizons has no ephemeris at this date. Its orientation uses an arbitrary display phase, not a measured attitude.",
